  stingers: ["Two meters. One song. Zero reasons.", "The needle agrees with the lights. Huge.", "Both meters say: yep.", "LEDs. Needle. Redundancy, baby.", "That's a plus three on the needle and a full stack on the lights. Same news, twice.", "M D F M. You better M D F M'in believe it! ... Who wrote this? This is bad. I am legit mad at you.", "M D F M. The beat goes on, and on, and on, and on. ... Why does it say on four times. Who wrote this. You're on thin ice.", "M D F M. Ninety nine point nine percent fresh! ... That's not a frequency, that's a yogurt. Who wrote this? See me after.", "M D F M. We put the M in M D F M. And the other M. ... I'm not reading the rest of this. Whoever wrote this, I know where you sit.", "M D F M. It's lit. It's fire. It's lit fire. ... That's arson. You wrote arson. I'm calling someone.", "M D F M. Turn it up! Turn it down! Turn it all around! ... These are just directions. Who wrote this. Go home.", "M D F M.", "M D F M. Keep it locked.", "Ninety nine point nine. M D F M H D.", "M D F M. Don't touch that knob. ... Okay, touch it a little.", "M D F M. Still here. Unfortunately for you.", "M D F M. That one was for the fruit flies."],
  tabitha: {"withData": ["It's {temp} degrees in {place}. Degrees were invented by a man called Fahrenheit, who was either very hot or very cold. History doesn't say which, because history is rubbish at weather.", "Today in {place} it's {cond}. Weather is what happens when the sky has feelings, and today the sky's feelings are: {cond}.", "The wind is {wind}. Wind is just air that's late for something. Like me. Except I was primping a pony. The wind has no excuse.", "{temp} degrees. Is that a lot? It depends who you ask. I asked a pigeon. It didn't answer, which I'm counting as a yes.", "It's {cond} in {place}. If you go outside, you'll be in it. If you stay inside, you'll be listening to me. So, really, there's no winning today.", "{place} is {cond}, at {temp} degrees. Some people say the weather is the same everywhere. Those people have never been anywhere. Neither have I. But I've seen pictures.", "In {place}, {temp} degrees and {cond}. The ancient Greeks had a god for weather. We have me. That's called progress."], "noData": ["I don't have the weather today. The weather has me. That's philosophy.", "Nobody's told me what the weather is. I'd look out the window, but this is a radio, and radios don't have windows. They have knobs. Three of them.", "The weather today is: outside. Inside, it's this. Back to you.", "Weather was invented in ancient times by farmers, who needed something to complain about that wasn't each other.", "I've been asked to give a forecast, but the future is unknowable, which is what makes it the future. If we knew it, it'd just be Thursday.", "Is it raining? Possibly. Is it sunny? Also possibly. Weather is like a cat in a box. Until you look outside, it's both. Please don't look. I'm enjoying this."], "thanks": ["Thanks, Tabitha.", "Thank you, Tabitha. I think.", "Tabitha Snatterbean, everybody.", "That was Tabitha. We're not sure either."]},
  sports: {"intro": ["Time for sports with Chip Nitro!", "Here's Chip Nitro with sports. Chip, you're on.", "Sports! With Chip Nitro! He asked us to say it like that."], "win": ["{team} beat the {opp}, {score} to {oscore}! I watched the whole thing! I didn't! I read it here! Still counts!", "Huge W for {team}! {score} to {oscore} over the {opp}! I'm gonna go run a lap! I'm not!", "{team} take down the {opp}, {score} to {oscore}! That's what we call a dub! I'm told nobody calls it that anymore! I do!"], "loss": ["{team} lost to the {opp}, {oscore} to {score}. Tough one. I'm not crying. You're crying. Have you tried crying? It's free.", "{team} fall to the {opp}, {oscore} to {score}. We don't talk about it. I just talked about it. Moving on.", "{opp} {oscore}, {team} {score}. Ooof. That's the sound I made. Ooof."], "live": ["{team} and the {opp} are going right now! {score} to {oscore}, {detail}! Why are you listening to the radio? Go watch it! Actually stay. I'm lonely.", "Live update! {team} {score}, {opp} {oscore}, {detail}! Anything can happen! Mostly sports! Sports can happen!"], "pre": ["{team} play the {opp} {when}. My prediction? A game. Somebody wins. Lock it in. Chip Nitro lock of the week.", "Coming up {when}: {team} versus the {opp}. I've got a good feeling. I've also got a bad feeling. I've got a lot of feelings, I'm a sports guy."], "noData": ["In the Browser Tab League, the Fruit Flies beat the Swatters three to one. The Swatters only showed up one time in ten, so honestly, what did they expect.", "No scores today. The scoreboard's in review. Rob's looking at it. Could be a while.", "Breaking news from the Knob Turning Championship. Gary went all the way to green. The crowd lost it. The crowd was Gary's dad.", "In the Spray Can Derby, Surf Swat edged out Honk-O-Cide by a nozzle. Huge upset. Clowns everywhere are devastated.", "The Eight Oh Eights slid past the Hi-Hats, a hundred and forty to nothing. The Hi-Hats were too quiet. Somebody took out all the high frequencies.", "Doug set a new record today. Fourteen hours of clapping. Still in the same kitchen. Somebody please call Doug's family."], "outro": ["Chip Nitro, sports! Back to you!", "That's sports! I'm Chip Nitro! I'm always Chip Nitro!", "Chip Nitro out! I'm not out. I'm still here. Okay now I'm out."]},
  weather: {"time": ["It's {time} on a {day}.", "M D F M time check. It's {time}.", "The time is {time}. We checked twice. We don't trust ourselves."], "timeMood": {"early": ["Too early for this. You're up anyway. Respect, sort of.", "The birds are up. You're up. Nobody asked either of you."], "morning": ["Coffee's working, or it isn't. Either way, here's a song.", "Morning productivity is a myth, but you're giving it a shot."], "midday": ["Lunch is soon, or lunch was. Only you know. We don't judge.", "Peak hours. You're peaking. Allegedly."], "afternoon": ["The afternoon slump is here. We're the soundtrack. Sorry.", "That three PM feeling. You know the one."], "evening": ["Shouldn't you be done by now? Rhetorical. We know you're not.", "It's after hours. The flies are clocking in."], "late": ["Why are you still working. Go to bed. ... After this song.", "It's late. Even Doug went home. Doug never goes home."]}, "withData": ["Right now in {place} it's {temp} degrees and {cond}. Perfect weather to stay inside and edit footage.", "Weather check. {place}, {temp} degrees, {cond}. You won't see any of it. You're at your desk.", "{place} is {cond} at {temp} degrees. Wind at {wind}. None of that affects your render times. Get back to it.", "It's {temp} out there in {place}, and {cond}. If you're thinking about going outside, a fly told us it's overrated.", "Current conditions in {place}: {cond}, {temp} degrees. Forecast for your inbox: heavy, with scattered review requests."], "noData": ["We don't have a window. Rob keeps us in a browser tab. Our best guess is partly cloudy with a chance of review.", "Weather update. We can't see outside. Can you? Is it nice? Don't tell us. We'll get jealous.", "Today's forecast: a high of one hundred percent CPU, with scattered fruit flies in the afternoon.", "The weather is whatever it is outside your window. We're a radio station in a work app. We tried our best.", "Our weather guy quit. He said nobody listens to the weather on a station that lives in a browser. He was right. Anyway, it's probably fine out."]},
